Meow fecis

==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|engenious}} {{qual|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|frm|ingénieux}}, from {{der|en|fro|engenious}}, from {{der|en|la|ingeniōsus|t=endowed with good natural capacity, gifted with genius}}, from {{m|la|ingenium|t=innate or natural quality, natural capacity, genius}}, from {{m|la|in|t=in}} + {{m|la|gignere|t=to produce}}, {{der|en|itc-ola|genere}}. See also {{m|en|engine}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-ingenious.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|iːniəs|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Displaying [[genius]] or [[brilliance]]; tending to [[invent]].
#: ''This fellow is '''ingenious'''; he fixed a problem I didn't even know I had.''
# Characterized by [[genius]]; cleverly done or [[contrived]].
#: ''That is an '''ingenious''' model of the atom.''
# [[witty|Witty]]; [[original]]; [[shrewd]]; [[adroit]]; [[keen]]; [[sagacious]].
#: ''He sent me an '''ingenious''' reply for an email.''

====Usage notes====
Do not confuse with [[ingenuous]].

====Synonyms====
* See also [[Thesaurus:witty]]
* See also [[Thesaurus:intelligent]]

